  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data exploration.** The data view `kibana_sample_data_logs` holds web-server access logs. The main fields are `timestamp`, `response` (with a `response.keyword` subfield), `clientip`, `bytes`, `extension`, `geo.dest`, `agent`, and `machine.os`.\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-fbbde856 Web logs overview\"** (ID `eff-fbbde856-web-logs-overview-3aee5c606f81`, default time range last year). It has 7 panels:\n- Total requests (metric)\n- Unique client IPs (metric)\n- Total bytes served (metric)\n- Requests over time (line, by `timestamp` date histogram)\n- Responses by status code (bar, terms on `response.keyword`)\n- Top request extensions (pie, terms on `extension.keyword`)\n- 5xx responses (ES|QL metric: `WHERE response.keyword RLIKE \"5..\"`)\n\n**Alert rule: \"EFF-fbbde856 5xx spike\"** (ID `7e31fa9d-ffb5-4ef4-8da4-f0aedbfb6773`). It is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`:\n- Query filters on `response.keyword` matching `5..`\n- Time field `timestamp`, window of 5 minutes\n- Fires when the count is greater than 10\n- Runs every 1 minute\n- Enabled. The alerting health check reports `ok`, with an encryption key configured and a secure connection.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- I couldn't query the data directly. `KIBANA_TEST_API_KEY` is empty in my shell, so my raw API calls returned 401. The 5xx panel and the rule both rely on `response.keyword` holding status codes as strings, which the field list suggests but I didn't confirm against the data. Check the 5xx panel shows a non-zero number, and check the rule's run history for errors.\n- I chose the 1-year default time range because I don't know when the sample data was loaded. Narrow it if you prefer.",
